WEBVTT

00:00:01.240 --> 00:00:07.170
Here's a cast on that may not be
the prettiest, but it's closed and fast.

00:00:07.240 --> 00:00:12.000
This is a Silver Reed 860 mid gauge
machine, and the setup would be similar to

00:00:12.066 --> 00:00:15.130
other Singer / Studio / Silver Reed machines.

00:00:15.200 --> 00:00:18.770
The cast on uses slip stitch.

00:00:18.840 --> 00:00:24.890
Slip settings on the machine means needles
in working or B position do not knit

00:00:24.960 --> 00:00:28.850
and the yarn passes under those needles.

00:00:28.920 --> 00:00:34.330
Let's get started by pulling
a few needles all the way out.

00:00:34.400 --> 00:00:39.010
With the carriage set for plain knitting,
the cam lever is on O,

00:00:39.080 --> 00:00:44.600
the side levers are on the triangle,
pass the carriage a couple of times

00:00:44.666 --> 00:00:47.970
and align the needles into B position.

00:00:48.040 --> 00:00:51.170
End with the carriage on the right.

00:00:51.240 --> 00:00:55.520
With your needle pusher,
pull every other needle to hold position

00:00:55.586 --> 00:01:00.440
or D or all the way out,
keeping those alternate

00:01:00.506 --> 00:01:03.320
needles in B position.

00:01:03.480 --> 00:01:08.080
Set the carriage to slip
by engaging both the side levers

00:01:08.146 --> 00:01:13.520
to the circle position
and set the cam lever to slip.

00:01:14.960 --> 00:01:18.760
Thread your carriage and knit to the left.

00:01:20.960 --> 00:01:26.560
Secure that tail with
a clip or a close pin.

00:01:29.280 --> 00:01:33.160
Notice how there are loops over every
other needle, and the needles that were

00:01:33.226 --> 00:01:36.570
in B position do not have loops.

00:01:36.640 --> 00:01:42.400
Now, this may seem a bit counterintuitive,
but that's the way slip works.

00:01:42.480 --> 00:01:47.370
With your carriage on the left,
pull the empty needles all the way out,

00:01:47.440 --> 00:01:52.930
knit across, and notice that these
needles now also have loops.

00:01:53.000 --> 00:01:54.850
Do this one more time.

00:01:54.920 --> 00:01:59.840
Pull those first same set
of needles and knit left.

00:01:59.920 --> 00:02:12.920
Then pull the alternate

00:02:12.986 --> 00:02:15.480
needles and knit right.

00:02:18.520 --> 00:02:23.000
Cancel slip by setting both side levers
to the triangle and the cam

00:02:23.066 --> 00:02:25.410
lever to O for plain knitting.

00:02:25.480 --> 00:02:28.730
Knit a few rows and take
a look at the edge.

00:02:28.800 --> 00:02:34.360
Not too pretty, but it is stable and fast,
and it works great for scraping on.

